---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="StripUnion's editorial policy for adult-platform reviews, comparisons, updates and affiliate disclosures.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell narrow"><span class="kicker">Editorial policy</span><h1>Editorial conclusions and commercial links are kept separate.</h1><p class="lead">Our review structure is designed around useful decision criteria rather than affiliate payouts or invented popularity scores.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section shell narrow article-body">
    <h2>Evaluation criteria</h2><p>Criteria vary by category. Live-cam reviews may focus on public access, tokens or credits, private interactions and privacy information; retail reviews should focus on catalog, delivery and customer policies. We avoid pretending one scoring model fits everything.</p>
    <h2>Source discipline</h2><p>Where a platform's official terms or help documentation materially supports a claim, we prefer primary sources and may link them directly. Volatile details such as prices, availability and terms should be checked again before publication or major updates.</p>
    <h2>Affiliate relationships</h2><p>An affiliate relationship can determine whether a commercial button is available, but it should not determine the editorial conclusion. If StripUnion does not have an approved affiliate relationship with a reviewed brand, we do not disguise another destination behind that brand's name.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material factual corrections should be incorporated into the relevant article and reflected in its update history when a formal corrections channel is introduced.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
